  "query_preview": "..\nThe Marianas are currently dry as a col produces divergent flow over\nthe area. However, scattered to numerous showers are visible on \neither side of the coastal waters and are expected to move in \nsometime late tonight or tomorrow with shower coverage highest over \nGuam and Rota. Light to moderate winds tomorrow will trend down by \nWednesday and potentially allow for island effect showers and \nthunderstorms to develop. Winds may stay light enough for continued \nisland effect for Tinian and Saipan Thursday before winds increase \nlate week and into the weekend as a new monsoonal surge potentially \nmoves into the Marianas. While a wetter period is expected late this \nweek with locally heavy showers possible, flooding and mudslide risk \nhas decreased at this time.",
